WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.620
I'm Nicole, I'm the current political action&nbsp;
co-chair of the Black Students Union here at&nbsp;&nbsp;MIT

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:12.300
I really got involved with the political&nbsp;
action last fall. I live in New House and on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.500
my floor in another community in new house 3.&nbsp;
I think someone was just fed up with the state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.940
of the kitchen and there were a lot of dirty&nbsp;
dirty dishes around and essentially they put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.320
up posters with a lot of violent language and it&nbsp;
also included the tired trope of starving children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.640
in Africa and it was about the nature of like&nbsp;
"Starving children in Africa would die to eat these&nbsp;scraps off your plates"

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.520
Often times what happens&nbsp;is the BSU exec will organize an emergency GBM&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.780
just to gather the opinions of people. It's also&nbsp;
kind of a check-in like "How are you guys doing, how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.900
does it affect you like -- community, like how are we&nbsp;
doing as a whole?" And then after that we kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:53.700
brainstorm solutions and what we want MIT admin&nbsp;
to do. Like last year I was not the student exec&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.100
but I worked really hard on writing the demands&nbsp;
after New House committee because I just thought it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:05.516
ridiculous that shit like this could happen. It&nbsp;
was so many nights of meetings and talking with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.516 --> 00:01:10.800
admin like even though I was choosing to put my&nbsp;
time into it, it's not like another extracurricular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.720
it's not like I'm choosing to go to soccer practice over&nbsp;
doing my homework, it's not like I'm going to like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.760
the business club. I am a black student, I'm&nbsp;
affected by this like instance of race-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.100
violence. I am calling an MIT to respond. It's&nbsp;
not my fault that I have to do that on top of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:31.860
being an MIT student. But officially we asked&nbsp;
for a couple things like a public apology,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:37.360
the discipline made known, the incident made public&nbsp;
to the MIT community. None of that happened [Music]

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:51.240
MIT is a money-making Institution, um in&nbsp;
meetings with admin it's never been hostile

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:57.180
but it feels like we're not being heard. They will&nbsp;
sit with you, um they'll have a meeting with you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:04.620
have a discussion and then after that either there's&nbsp;
no follow-up or they tell you "Sorry, no." 

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.620
Like I know Boston is one of the most racist cities in&nbsp;
America-- that's not it. We are on MIT's campus and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.320
in Simmons actually last year a student walked&nbsp;
into a room full of, you know, people of color&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:22.680
and just called them slurs and then walked out. Why&nbsp;
do I have to go through MIT being subjected to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.560
and MIT does nothing about it. And it's really&nbsp;
hard because people are saying like "Oh you didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.460
have to be BSU co-chair, you don't have to get&nbsp;
involved in BSU exec, you don't have to completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:38.160
disengage from your identity but you don't need&nbsp;
to do activism. If I don't do it who is going to do&nbsp;it?

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.740
Because MIT is not fighting for black students,&nbsp;
and I've heard that from admin, like they will not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:49.140
act unless we as students push them to act.  So yes,
I don't have to be co-chair, I don't have to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:55.680
on BSU exec but that means there will be no place&nbsp;
for black students at MIT, and I cannot have that

